# Fblthp, "ward {2}": the positive control. Bot2's Black Lotus makes three red, so after the Bolt it can pay {2}, the ward
# trigger's counter is paid off and the Bolt kills Fblthp. With Fblthp gone, "the top card of your library has plot" and "you
# may plot nonland cards from the top of your library" are over (CR 611.3a, 113.6): on turn three, with Mox Ruby's {R} to pay
# for it, the Lightning Bolt on top of Bot1's library is not offered for plot.

